{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1559421-what-other-magical-materials-have-you-used","id":1559421,"title":"What Other Magical Materials Have You Used?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-14T17:38:53-07:00","id":1559421,"title":"What Other Magical Materials Have You Used?","content":"We all know the big five magical materials - jade, moonsilver, orichalcum, soulsteel, and starmetal. The books cite these as the strongest magical materials for artifact creation, and therefore they form the basis of basically every artifact we've had written up.<br /> <br /> Still, other &quot;exotic&quot; ingredients are referenced quite a bit in the text, both in the abstract sense that such artifacts exist and as cores for many example artifacts that had some of the big five materials composited with them to make them more suitable to the Exalted. Arms of the Chosen lists a bunch, with varying rarity - bones, horns and sinews of behemoths are fairly common, but you also get really out-there stuff like the brush of the artist god who painted extra colors onto sunlight, or the gem with the ghost-court trapped inside.<br /> <br /> So that's what I wanna talk about today - in the original artifacts from your games (whether introduced by the ST, or bought or built by the players) what have been your favorite exotic materials used for artifice? Have you ever utilized any artifacts that were of entirely-exotic material, not alloyed or overlaid with any of the big five materials? Share your stories!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T05:51:15-07:00","id":1559428,"title":"","content":"My sidereal had his armour made out of the silk cocoon of some Grass Spiders that tried to eat him as a child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T04:31:32-07:00","id":1560705,"title":"","content":"I suspect grass/essence/giant spider silk is among the most used esoteric components that is not one of the magical materials. Or maybe my PoV is skewed by a dragon-blooded PC belonging to a cadet house of the Dynasty that has a centuries-long alliance with a brood of spiders they have both reared and subtly enhanced through sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> Anyway, a bunch of stuff gathered from high-level demesnes, the discarded skin of a serpent god, memories of a life never lived stolen from a Getimian, quicksilver thousand-reforged into the most crimson cynnabar (in dedication to Ululaya the Red Moon of Kimbery) and other things i forget.<br /> <br /> Coming up with them and actual uses is half the fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}